  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for cyrus-sasl",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for cyrus-sasl fixes the following issues:\n\nSecurity issue fixed:\n\n- CVE-2026-107161: Heap buffer overflow in cyrus-sasl add_to_challenge() allows malicious server to crash or compromise\n  DIGEST-MD5 clients (bsc#1284687).\n\nNon security issues fixed:\n\n- Fix cyrus-sasl package failing to build with GCC 14 (bsc#1221863).\n- Replace insecure MD5 with ephemeral HMAC-SHA256 (bsc#1247498).\n- Make DIGEST-MD5 work with openssl3 (bsc#1230111).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
